k useEffect has a missing dependency: 'requestPermission'. Either include it or remove the dependency array.","ArrayExpression",["185"],"'Spacing' is defined but never used.",["186"],"'Dimensions' is defined but never used.",["187"],"'GestureResponderEvent' is defined but never used.",["188"],"'Wifi' is defined but never used.",["189"],"'frameUri' is assigned a value but never used.","'setFrameUri' is assigned a value but never used.","'setCustomPort' is assigned a value but never used.","react-hooks/refs","Error: Cannot access refs during render\n\nReact refs are values that are not needed for rendering. Refs should only be accessed outside of render, such as in event handlers or effects. Accessing a ref value (the `current` property) during render can cause your component not to update as expected (https://react.dev/reference/react/useRef).\n\nC:\\Projects\\VediPocketPC\\vedi-pocketpc-desktop\\veddi-pocketpc\\components\\DesktopViewport.tsx:105:25\n  103 |   // PanResponder to handle dragging finger on Desktop Viewport to move PC cursor\n  104 |   const panResponder = useRef(\n> 105 |     PanResponder.create({\n      |                         ^\n> 106 |       onStartShouldSetPanResponder: () => interactive && touchMode === 'click',\n      | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n> 107 |       onMoveShouldSetPanResponder: () => interactive && touchMode === 'click',\n      …\n      | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n> 135 |       },\n      | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n> 136 |     })\n      | ^^^^^^ Passing a ref to a function may read its value during render\n  137 |   ).current;\n  138 |\n  139 |   // Determine effective target IP and Port","react-hooks/immutability","Error: This value cannot be modified\n\nModifying a value previously passed as an argument to a hook is not allowed. Consider moving the modification before calling the hook.\n\nC:\\Projects\\VediPocketPC\\vedi-pocketpc-desktop\\veddi-pocketpc\\components\\DesktopViewport.tsx:182:7\n  180 |       const ws = new WebSocket(wsUrl);\n  181 |       ws.binaryType = 'arraybuffer';\n> 182 |       wsRef.current = ws;\n      |       ^^^^^ `wsRef` cannot be modified\n  183 |\n  184 |       ws.onopen = () => {\n  185 |         console.log('[ScreenViewport] Connected to screen stream');","React Hook useCallback has missing dependencies: 'selectedFps', 'selectedRes.h', and 'selectedRes.w'. Either include them or remove the dependency array.",["190"],"react-hooks/set-state-in-effect","Error: Calling setState synchronously within an effect can trigger cascading renders\n\nEffects are intended to synchronize state between React and external systems such as manually updating the DOM, state management libraries, or other platform APIs. In general, the body of an effect should do one or both of the following:\n* Update external systems with the latest state from React.\n* Subscribe for updates from some external system, calling setState in a callback function when external state changes.\n\nCalling setState synchronously within an effect body causes cascading renders that can hurt performance, and is not recommended. (https://react.dev/learn/you-might-not-need-an-effect).\n\nC:\\Projects\\VediPocketPC\\vedi-pocketpc-desktop\\veddi-pocketpc\\components\\DesktopViewport.tsx:234:5\n  232 |   // Auto-start screen stream on component mount & clean up on unmount\n  233 |   useEffect(() => {\n> 234 |     startStream();\n      |     ^^^^^^^^^^^ Avoid calling setState() directly within an effect\n  235 |     return () => {\n  236 |       stopStream();\n  237 |     };","Error: Cannot access refs during render\n\nReact refs are values that are not needed for rendering. Refs should only be accessed outside of render, such as in event handlers or effects. Accessing a ref value (the `current` property) during render can cause your component not to update as expected (https://react.dev/reference/react/useRef).\n\nC:\\Projects\\VediPocketPC\\vedi-pocketpc-desktop\\veddi-pocketpc\\components\\DesktopViewport.tsx:307:13\n  305 |       {/* Screen Viewport Canvas */}\n  306 |       <View\n> 307 |         {...panResponder.panHandlers}\n      |             ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ Cannot access ref value during render\n  308 |         style={[styles.viewportFrame, isFullscreen && styles.fullscreenFrame]}\n  309 |       >\n  310 |         {hasFrame ? (",{"messageId":"191","data":"192","fix":"193","desc":"194"},{"messageId":"191","data":"195","fix":"196","desc":"197"},{"desc":"198","fix":"199"},{"messageId":"191","data":"200","fix":"201","desc":"202"},{"messageId":"191","data":"203","fix":"204","desc":"205"},{"messageId":"191","data":"206","fix":"207","desc":"208"},{"messageId":"191","data":"209","fix":"210","desc":"211"},{"desc":"212","fix":"213"},"removeUnusedVar",{"varName":"214"},{"range":"215","text":"216"},"Remove unused variable \"describePairError\".",{"varName":"217"},{"range":"218","text":"216"},"Remove unused variable \"Tv\".","Update the dependencies array to be: [permission, requestPermission]",{"range":"219","text":"220"},{"varName":"221"},{"range":"222","text":"216"},"Remove unused variable \"Spacing\".",{"varName":"223"},{"range":"224","text":"216"},"Remove unused variable \"Dimensions\".",{"varName":"225"},{"range":"226","text":"216"},"Remove unused variable \"GestureResponderEvent\".",{"varName":"227"},{"range":"228","text":"216"},"Remove unused variable \"Wifi\".","Update the dependencies array to be: [stopStream, targetIp, targetPort, selectedRes.w, selectedRes.h, selectedFps]",{"range":"229","text":"230"},"describePairError",[535,554],"","Tv",[83,87],[1093,1105],"[permission, requestPermission]","Spacing",[268,277],"Dimensions",[160,174],"GestureResponderEvent",[174,199],"Wifi",[349,357],[6888,6922],"[stopStream, targetIp, targetPort, selectedRes.w, selectedRes.h, selectedFps]"]